<title>ARGENTINA: Argentines suspend &quot;Trainspotting&quot; after threats.</title>
<headline>Argentines suspend &quot;Trainspotting&quot; after threats.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine distributor of the controversial British film &quot;Trainspotting&quot; said he had called off the film's Buenos Aires premiere planned for next week after receiving anonymous threats.</p>
<p>The distributor said late on Saturday that telephone callers had mentioned an &quot;anti-drug addiction league&quot; that opposed the showing of the film.</p>
<p>&quot;Trainspotting,&quot; one of British cinema's biggest-ever box office hits, graphically tells the story of a group of Scottish drug addicts. Opponents of the film say it glamorizes the use of drugs.</p>
<p>The Argentine distributor said the decision to call off next Thursday's planned screening in Buenos Aires was not definitive, the state-owned Telam news agency reported.</p>
